    <DataNode elementId="_17-BETA-HYDROXY-5ALPHA-ANDROSTAN-3-O" textLabel="5α-dihydrotestosterone" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="NVKAWKQGWWIWPM-ABEVXSGRSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="400" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, zhang, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: 17-BETA-HYDROXYANDROSTAN-3-ONE 5&amp;alpha;-Dihydrotestosterone| (DHT) is a metabolite of |FRAME: TESTOSTERONE|, and a more potent androgen than testosterone in that it binds more strongly to androgen receptors. It is regarded as the most potent natural androgen. DHT is synthesized in peripheral tissue such as the prostate or skin by the 5&amp;alpha;-reduction of |FRAME: TESTOSTERONE|, with little amounts in the circulation |CITS: [5671431][4384673]|. It plays a crucial role in sexual differentiation of the male genitalia during embryogenesis and maturation of the penis and scrotum at puberty. It is also important for the development of pubic hair and the development and maintenance of the prostate gland and seminal vesicles in adult males.</Comment>
